Kubernetes Services
Service is a method for exposing Pods in your cluster.
Each Pod gets its own IP address, but we need access using the Node IP.
To access Pods internally within the cluster, we use ClusterIP.
If the Service type is NodePort or LoadBalancer, it can also be accessed from outside the cluster.
Services help decouple Pods from the network topology, making applications easier to manage and scale.
Types of Kubernetes Services
   ClusterIP   - expose pods within the cluster it provides stable ip address by using the statble ip we can access application internally (withinserver ) will use in db server 
   NodePort    -expose pods it provides stable ip & node port node port range (30K TO 32767)  TO BROWSE OVER INTERNET WILL ISE NODE PORT
   LoadBalancer -EXPOSE POD, it provides stable ip , node port & DNS (www.flm.com)  while creating laod balancer so here kubernetes will communicate with cloud provider
Kubernetes Service Types
    Service Type	IP Details	Access Type
   ClusterIP	Stable IP	Internal
    NodePort	Stable IP + Node Port	Internal & External
    LoadBalancer	Stable IP + Node Port + DNS	Internal & External
Simple Understanding
  ClusterIP  ---> Used for communication inside the cluster only.
   NodePort  --->Exposes application using: NodeIP:Port  Accessible from outside the cluster.
LoadBalancer  --->Creates an external load balancer with DNS Mostly used in cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, GCP.

Note : In nodeport all requests goto single server & in loadbalncer all requests destribute server equvally
